<PageLayout
  title="TotalRecalls FAQ"
  description="Frequently asked questions about TotalRecalls: pricing, providers, privacy, refunds, and how downloads work."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "FAQ" }]}
>
  <h1>FAQ</h1>

  <dl>
    <dt>What is TotalRecalls?</dt>
    <dd>A small Windows app that downloads your AI chat history from ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini (Google Takeout), Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat into local Markdown + JSON files you own forever. See <a href="/how-it-works/">How It Works</a>.</dd>

    <dt>How much does it cost?</dt>
    <dd><span data-tr-price>$24<span class="tr-usd">USD</span></span> launch price. One-time purchase. No subscription. No monthly "AI archive" fee. A Free Tier is available now — download the app and test it before paying. The Free Tier is limited to 3 AI providers and 5 conversations per download. See <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a> for the full breakdown.</dd>

    <dt>Do I need an account?</dt>
    <dd>No. TotalRecalls does not require a TotalRecalls account. You sign in only to the AI providers you already use.</dd>

    <dt>Do you store my chats or tokens?</dt>
    <dd>No. Your AI session tokens stay on your machine. We never host your chats, your downloads, or your credentials. Read the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</dd>

    <dt>Does TotalRecalls run in the cloud?</dt>
    <dd>No. It's a local Windows app. Downloads land in a folder you choose on your PC.</dd>

    <dt>What providers are supported?</dt>
    <dd>ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini (via Google Takeout import), Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat. See the <a href="/guides/">Guides</a> for per-provider walkthroughs.</dd>

    <dt>How do downloads work?</dt>
    <dd>
      <ol>
        <li>Open the app</li>
        <li>Pick a provider</li>
        <li>Sign in locally (or choose a Gemini Takeout folder)</li>
        <li>Pick an output folder and click <em>Download</em></li>
      </ol>
      Your Markdown + JSON files are written straight to disk on your machine.
    </dd>

    <dt>Does this replace official downloads?</dt>
    <dd>No. It complements them. TotalRecalls catches conversations the official download tools miss (shared links, archived conversations, partial histories) and writes them in a single Markdown + JSON format you can grep, version, and search.</dd>

    <dt>Is the app safe?</dt>
    <dd>Yes. The app runs locally on your Windows machine, never connects to a TotalRecalls server, never hosts your chats, and ships with no telemetry. You can verify by inspecting network traffic with Wireshark if you want.</dd>

    <dt>Does it work on Mac?</dt>
    <dd>Not yet. Windows 10/11 today. Developing an application for Linux and Apple (macOS) is in the works.</dd>

    <dt>Does it work on mobile?</dt>
    <dd>No. Windows only.</dd>

    <dt>What's inside the ZIP?</dt>
    <dd>Two files: <code>TotalRecalls.exe</code> (the app, portable &mdash; no installer) and <code>README.txt</code> (release notes + quick-start). See the <a href="/download/">Download page</a>.</dd>

    <dt>Will future features cost extra?</dt>
    <dd>The $24<span class="tr-usd">USD</span> launch price covers the core download tool, including free updates to it for the life of the product. Advanced features (Obsidian/Notion sync, RAG containers, multi-device memory) are separate add-on purchases — add-ons you own keep getting updates. Smart Search Engine is available now as a Pro add-on.</dd>

    <dt>Do I need the Smart Search Engine add-on?</dt>
    <dd>No. TotalRecalls Pro downloads and saves everything without it. Smart Search Engine is for people who want to find things inside a large archive.</dd>

    <dt>Can I buy Smart Search Engine without Pro?</dt>
    <dd>No. It works on the Library that Pro builds. The bundle gives you both.</dd>

    <dt>Does Smart Search Engine upload my conversations?</dt>
    <dd>No. It runs on your PC. The only internet use is a one-time download of the search model during setup.</dd>

    <dt>Does it work offline?</dt>
    <dd>Yes, after setup.</dd>

    <dt>Do I need an AI model or LM Studio?</dt>
    <dd>No. Search and retrieval-only chat work without one. A local model is optional, if you want written answers.</dd>

    <dt>What do I need to run Smart Search Engine?</dt>
    <dd>Windows 10 or 11, about 8 GB of RAM and about 2 GB of free disk space. No graphics card.</dd>

    <dt>How does Smart Search Engine stay up to date?</dt>
    <dd>It re-indexes automatically after downloads and on a schedule.</dd>

    <dt>Does Smart Search Engine work with every provider?</dt>
    <dd>It searches all eight: ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat. Search quality for non-English conversations may vary.</dd>

    <dt>Is Smart Search Engine a subscription?</dt>
    <dd>No. It’s a one-time purchase: $39 at launch (regular $59). There is no subscription.</dd>

    <dt>Is Smart Search Engine included in Pro updates?</dt>
    <dd>Pro’s free core updates do not include Smart Search Engine. It is a separate purchase, with free updates within version 1.</dd>

    <dt>Is there a bundle?</dt>
    <dd>Yes. Pro + Smart Search Engine is $55 at launch (regular $89). If you already own Pro, add Smart Search Engine for $31 at launch.</dd>

    <dt>When do the launch prices end?</dt>
    <dd>On [DATE]. After that, Pro is $48, Smart Search Engine is $59 and the bundle is $89.</dd>

    <dt>What’s your refund policy for Smart Search Engine?</dt>
    <dd>30 days, no questions asked.</dd>

    <dt>What do I get today, and what is coming?</dt>
    <dd>Today: search by meaning, keyword or both; plain-English questions turned into SQL; chat with your archive; Obsidian and Notion connections; automatic re-index. Coming as free updates for Smart Search Engine buyers: the PII Scrubber, fine-tuning export, Consensus Auditor, Knowledge Graph and embedding benchmark.</dd>

    <dt>Does it work with free-tier accounts?</dt>
    <dd>Yes. TotalRecalls works with free-tier ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat accounts. Gemini requires a Google account with Takeout enabled.</dd>

    <dt>Are images, code blocks, and attachments included?</dt>
    <dd>Chat text and code blocks download as Markdown; attachment references are preserved alongside (e.g. sources.json). The binary files themselves stay in your provider account.</dd>

    <dt>What happens when a provider changes its site?</dt>
    <dd>TotalRecalls is updated to keep downloads working when providers change their interfaces. New versions are listed in the <a href="/release-notes/">Release Notes</a>.</dd>

    <dt>How large can downloads get?</dt>
    <dd>Practically unlimited. Downloads are streamed to disk, so a 50,000-message archive works the same as a 500-message one. The only limit is your free disk space.</dd>

    <dt>Can I get help?</dt>
    <dd>Yes. Email <a href="mailto:support@totalrecalls.app">support@totalrecalls.app</a>, or see the <a href="/support/">Support</a> page.</dd>
  </dl>


  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={jsonLd} />
</PageLayout>
